Normalize native-endian Cairo image uploads before sending them to WebRender.

On big-endian, some Cairo-backed fallback/image paths can expose explicit
A8R8G8B8/X8R8G8B8 surfaces. WebRender descriptors do not support those native
byte-order formats directly; letting them reach IPC produces an invalid
ImageFormat value and crashes while serializing OpAddImage. Convert those
4-byte native ARGB/XRGB buffers to WebRender's BGRA/BGRX byte layout at the
resource-update boundary.

This is a pure host-byte-order boundary fix and is guarded with the compiler's
__BYTE_ORDER__ condition.

Dependency: apply after SPARC-01-cairo-surface-format.patch. This patch handles
the WebRender upload boundary for native Cairo formats made visible by the base
format-contract patch.

